,null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Outlook it expresses"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"direction-neutral, expecting a large move"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Opens with"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"a debit"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Best case"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Unlimited on the upside, bounded by zero on the downside"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Worst case"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Total premium paid, if the underlying settles exactly at the strike"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Breakeven"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Strike plus total premium, and strike minus total premium"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Exposures"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"delta neutral · gamma positive · theta negative · vega positive"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-card border px-[18px] py-4 transition-colors duration-panel ease-standard bg-card border-border shadow-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-3 flex items-center gap-2","children":["$undefined",["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold leading-tight","children":["Lesson",false]}],false]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted [&_h1]:mb-2 [&_h1]:text-base [&_h1]:font-bold [&_h1]:text-text [&_h2]:mb-1.5 [&_h2]:mt-5 [&_h2]:text-[13px] [&_h2]:font-bold [&_h2]:text-text [&_h3]:mb-1 [&_h3]:mt-4 [&_h3]:text-[12px] [&_h3]:font-semibold [&_h3]:text-text [&_p]:mb-2.5 [&_strong]:font-semibold [&_strong]:text-text [&_ul]:mb-2.5 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_ol]:mb-2.5 [&_ol]:list-decimal [&_ol]:pl-5 [&_li]:mb-1 [&_code]:rounded [&_code]:bg-bg [&_code]:px-1 [&_code]:py-0.5 [&_code]:font-mono [&_code]:text-[11px] [&_code]:text-text [&_table]:mb-3 [&_table]:w-full [&_table]:text-left [&_table]:text-[11.5px] [&_th]:border-b [&_th]:border-border [&_th]:pb-1 [&_th]:pr-3 [&_th]:font-semibold [&_th]:text-text [&_td]:border-b [&_td]:border-border [&_td]:py-1 [&_td]:pr-3 [&_td]:align-top [&_a]:text-teal hover:[&_a]:underline [&_blockquote]:border-l-2 [&_blockquote]:border-border2 [&_blockquote]:pl-3 [&_blockquote]:italic","children":[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"Long Straddle"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":"A long call and a long put at the same strike, same expiry — almost always at the\r\nmoney. The position has no directional view; it has a view about magnitude."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"children":"The structure"}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":"Two long legs, one strike. Total premium is the sum of both, and that total\r\nis the maximum loss."}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":"Delta is roughly zero at entry because the call's positive delta and the put's\r\nnegative delta offset. The position is not betting on direction. It is betting\r\nthat realised movement will exceed what implied volatility has priced in."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"children":"What it is exposed to"}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Gamma"}]," strongly positive. This is the engine. As the underlying moves in\r\neither direction, the position acquires delta in the direction of the move —\r\nit gets longer as price rises and shorter as price falls. That self-correcting\r\nproperty is what produces gain from movement alone."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-4",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Theta"}]," strongly negative, and it is paid twice. Two long options both decay,\r\nand both are at the money where extrinsic value is greatest. An at-the-money\r\nstraddle in the final days of a weekly contract loses value at a rate that\r\nsurprises people who have only held single options."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-5",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Vega"}]," strongly positive. The position gains if implied volatility rises even\r\nwithout the underlying moving."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-6",{"children":"The tension between gamma and theta is the whole trade. Gamma pays when the\r\nunderlying moves; theta charges rent for the privilege of holding gamma. The\r\nposition is profitable when realised volatility exceeds implied volatility over\r\nthe holding period — that is the actual condition, stated precisely."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"children":"Payoff"}],"\n",["$","p","p-7",{"children":"At expiry the position is worth the distance between the underlying and the\r\nstrike, in either direction. It is profitable beyond strike ± total premium.\r\nMaximum loss occurs at exactly the strike, where both legs expire worthless."}],"\n",["$","p","p-8",{"children":["The breakevens are wide. Both legs' premiums must be recovered by movement in\r\n",["$","em","em-0",{"children":"one"}]," direction, since only one leg can finish in the money. This is why a\r\nstraddle needs a genuinely large move, not merely a directional one."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-3",{"children":"Indian market specifics"}],"\n",["$","p","p-9",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"The event problem."}]," Straddles are most often bought before scheduled events\r\n— results, RBI policy, budget, election counting. Implied volatility rises into\r\nthose events precisely because everyone anticipates movement. The straddle\r\nbought the day before is paying an inflated premium, and when the event passes,\r\nimplied volatility collapses regardless of outcome. The underlying can move\r\nsubstantially and the straddle can still lose, because the vega loss exceeds\r\nthe gamma gain."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-10",{"children":["This is the most reliable way to lose money on a correct forecast, and it is\r\ncovered in ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"volatility/volatility-crush.md"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-11",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Weekly decay."}]," With only NIFTY carrying weekly contracts on NSE since the\r\nNovember 2024 rationalisation, weekly straddles concentrate in one instrument.\r\nA NIFTY weekly straddle held from Wednesday into Tuesday expiry faces\r\nnear-vertical theta in its final sessions."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-12",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"India VIX"}]," is the reference for whether the straddle is being bought cheap\r\nor dear. An at-the-money straddle's price is approximately the market's\r\nexpected move over the contract's life — comparing that implied move against\r\nthe underlying's recent realised range is the comparison the position depends\r\non."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-13",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Cost."}]," Two legs in, two out, plus STT on both sold legs at exit. On a weekly\r\nNIFTY straddle these costs are small relative to premium, but on an illiquid\r\nstock straddle the bid-ask on two legs can consume a meaningful share of the\r\nexpected move."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-4",{"children":"How it typically fails"}],"\n",["$","p","p-14",{"children":"Buying before an event and holding through it, as above. Second: holding\r\nthrough a quiet period and paying theta on both legs for days while the\r\nunderlying oscillates within the breakevens — being right that a move is coming\r\nbut wrong about when, which for a decaying position is the same as being wrong."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-5",{"children":"Related"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/volatility/long-strangle.md"}]," — cheaper, wider breakevens, same idea"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/volatility/short-straddle.md"}]," — the other side of this trade"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"volatility/historical-vs-implied.md"}]," — the comparison that determines the outcome"]}],"\n"]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[10px] leading-relaxed text-faint","children":["Educational material describing how a structure behaves. Not a recommendation, not a signal, and not personalised advice. Source: ",["$","code",null,{"className":"font-mono","children":"docs/learning/strategies/volatility/long-straddle.md"}]]}]]}],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children","$4","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[[null,["$","$L6",null,{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyl